{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>You shall not be able to consume them quickly</b> — He promises that HaShem will destroy them all and will send the hornet among them to destroy those remaining and those hidden, and behold all of them will perish. But He said that He will not consume them in war in a single day, nor drive them from the land in a single year, lest the land become desolate and the beasts of the field multiply against you. He further adds a promise that these remaining ones will not be numerous, but HaShem will throw them into great confusion and most of them will perish by Israel's hand. And so He said (Deuteronomy 9:3), 'He will destroy them and He will subdue them before you, and you shall dispossess them and destroy them quickly' — that most of them will perish quickly, not that they will be entirely consumed, until you increase and inherit the land."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:46:37.552912017Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}